# THE TRACES ARE NOT COMMITTED, and the summaries are.
#
# A trace is 50-80 KB and there is one per game; the corpus is hundreds of
# games, and every byte of it is a deterministic function of (build, scenario,
# seed, arm) — `--nodes` is what that mode is for. So the traces are
# REGENERATED, never stored: every reproduction in BEHAVIOUR-AUDIT-3.md prints
# the single command that rebuilds its own, and `scripts/wide-corpus.sh` will
# re-record any game whose summary is missing and skip every one that is not.
#
# The JSON summaries ARE committed: they are what `ab-compare.js` and
# `wide-corpus.js pair` subtract, they are small, and a later build's numbers
# are only meaningful against a recorded earlier build's.
logs/
tmp/

# The two concatenations `ab-compare.js` reads are `cat json/*-<arm>.jsonl`,
# rebuilt by the recorder on every run. Storing them would store the corpus
# twice.
wide-mirror.jsonl
wide-material-only.jsonl
